<title>SINGAPORE: VICOM 1st-half net profits down 36.8 pct.</title>
<headline>VICOM 1st-half net profits down 36.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>(millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    0.96  vs  1.52</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (cents)	1.20  vs  2.53*</p>
<p>    Turnover				3.34  vs  3.95</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest     0.30  vs  0.15</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	    0.49  vs  0.27</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			1.30  vs  2.15</p>
<p>    Tax				     0.34  vs  0.63</p>
<p>Note - Vehicle inspection company VICOM Ltd began trading on the Stock Exchange of Singapore on October 11, 1995.</p>
<p>* The year-ago group share figure is adjusted for a share split and bonus issue.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
